    "q-61916": {
      "dom_id": "step-q61916",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "A watch collector bought a watch for $$50.$ They estimate that the value of the watch increases at a rate of $8%$ every decade. According to this estimate, what will be the price of the watch after $3$ decades? Round your answer to the nearest dollar.",
      "worked_solution": "The price of the watch $y(t)$ grows exponentially with a growth rate of $8%.$\n\nThe formula for exponential growth (in terms of a growth rate $r$) is\n\n$$\ny=a(1+r)^{t}.\n$$\n\nWe have:\n\n- $a=50$ dollars is the original price of the watch.\n\n- $r=0.08$ is the growth rate ($8%$ expressed as a decimal).\n\n- $t=$ the time, in decades.\n\nTherefore, the correct expression for $y$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =50\\cdot (1+0.08)^{t} \\\\  & =50\\cdot (1.08)^{t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating the function at $t=3$ gives the value of the watch after $3$ decades.\n\n$$\ny(3)=50\\cdot (1.08)^{3}≈63\n$$\n\nTherefore, the value of the watch after $3$ decades will be approximately $$63.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
