    "q-317613": {
      "dom_id": "step-q317613",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "A video was posted on a streaming platform with $50$ initial views. An exponential model estimates that at the end of each hour after the video was posted, the number of views increased by $120%$ of the number of views at the end of the previous hour.\n\nAccording to this model, how many views are there estimated to be after $3$ hours?",
      "worked_solution": "The number of views $V(t)$ grows exponentially with a growth rate of $120%.$\n\nLet's write down what we know:\n\n- $a=50$ is the total number of views initially\n\n- $r=1.2$ is the growth rate ($120%$ expressed as a decimal)\n\n- $t=$ the time (in hours) after the video was posted\n\nThe formula for exponential growth (in terms of a growth rate $r$) is\n\n$$\nV=a(1+r)^{t}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct expression for $V(t)$ is\n\n$$\nV=50\\cdot (1+1.2)^{t}.\n$$\n\nSimplifying the above, we get\n\n$$\nV(t)=50\\cdot (2.2)^{t}.\n$$\n\nTo find the total number of views after $3$ hours, we evaluate the above for $t=3:$\n\n$$\nV(3)=50\\cdot (2.2)^{3}≈532\n$$\n\nTherefore, the estimated number of views after $3$ hours is $532.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
